  "name": "Fukera and shellela (Amhara war-boast and war chant)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Martial vocal genres of the Amhara highlands of Gondar, Gojjam and Shewa. In fukera a man declaims a boast of his own bravery and deeds, and in shellela a singer chants heroic verses that once roused warriors before battle; both are still performed at weddings, holidays and public ceremonies, and the saxophonist Getatchew Mekurya adapted the shellela style to his instrument.",
